 "version": 1,
 "name": "Boss MT-2 Metal Zone",
 "description": "Boss MT-2 Metal Zone (1991) as drawn in the Roland service notes (MT BOARD 7527552000, pcb 22930117RT). 2SK184 source-follower input -> 2SK118 effect switch (ON) -> IC3b pre-distortion shaping: non-inverting, 220 k // 100 p feedback, and to ground C034 0.027 in series with a transistor gyrator (Q010 2SC3378 emitter follower: C035 0.01 from the C034 node to the base, R053 47 k base to +4.5 V, R046 2.2 k from the emitter back to the C034 node, R054 10 k emitter load) -> a 952 Hz band-pass, about +36 dB peak -> R045/R042 divider with C031 (340 Hz) -> IC3a gain x2...x252 (DIST 250 kA) -> 2.2 k into a 1SS133 pair to ground -> R032/R031/C023 shelf -> IC4b post-shaping with two more transistor gyrators (4.9 kHz and 105 Hz peaks) -> IC4a unity inverter -> IC1a High/Low cut-boost (High shelf 2.2 k/10 n, Low = IC1b op-amp gyrator 105 Hz) -> IC2a Middle cut/boost with an IC2b-driven Wien bridge swept by the dual-gang MID FREQ -> LEVEL 50 kA -> 2SK118 effect switch (ON) -> 2SC3378 emitter-follower output. The flip-flop footswitch logic, the CHECK LED and the bypass switch Q003 (OFF in the effect state) are not modelled; the bypass buffer Q004 is, because it loads the input buffer. Engine notes: the +4.5 V rail (R056/R057 with C040 + C019, 200 uF) is a supply cut, which splits the single 33-port group into eleven stage groups (CPU 30.8 % -> 13.7 % of a core at 96 kHz, gate unchanged within 0.7 % NRMSE). The solver is pinned to nodal DK because with the cut the automatic WDF choice for the clipper group (C027..R029) outputs a silent clip node (engine bug, reported).",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Boss MT-2 Service Notes, Apr 1991 (Roland): MT BOARD circuit diagram (assy 7527552000, pcb 22930117RT 1/2 and VR board 2/2) and parts list (M5218AL IC1-4; 2SC3378GR / 2SC2240GR, 2SC2458GR, 2SK184GR / 2SK117GR, 2SK118Y; S5500G, 1SS133, RD5.6EB3, LN-28RP; pots 100kW+100kW HIGH/LOW, 50kCx2+100kW MIDDLE, 250kA DIST, 50kA LEVEL)",
   "url": "https://www.synfo.nl/servicemanuals/Boss/BOSS_MT-2_SERVICE_NOTES.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "Hobby Hour, Boss MT-2 Metal Zone schematic (clean single-page copy of the same diagram; used to cross-read the VR board and the gyrator transistors)",
   "url": "https://www.hobby-hour.com/electronics/s/schematics/boss-mt2-metal-zone-schematic.png"
  },
  {
   "title": "Electric Druid, 'Boss MT-2 Metal Zone pedal analysis' (stage values, the 106 Hz / 7.2 kHz / 340 Hz / 48 Hz corners, gain x2-x252, the gyrator tables 4898 Hz Q 2.2 and 105 Hz Q 14.6 / 3.1, +/-20 dB High/Low, +/-15 dB Mid from 240 Hz to 4.7/6.3 kHz, and the published pre-distortion response with its ~1 kHz peak, ~36 dB per the article's comments)",
   "url": "https://electricdruid.net/boss-mt-2-metal-zone-pedal-analysis/"
  },
  {
   "title": "Mitsubishi M5218AL/P/FP datasheet: Gvo 110 dB, fT 7 MHz, SR 3.0 V/us typ",
   "url": "https://www.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/pdf/908/MITSUBISHI/M5218.html"
  }
 ],
